    leanNote: "In the Kripke semantics of lean/PIKripke.lean (model in lean/PIOQ_KIE.lean). Three worlds: the actual world 0 sees 1 and 2; 1 and 2 see only themselves. Two entities, and a base type d with two items; identity of entities and of items of d is identity at every world; ≈ is identity of types. A function from propositions to entities and one from propositions to items of d are identified (at every world) just in case they have the same graph and the first is an item at the actual world. Within a type, identity at a world is the Kripke identity.",
